i),$ then $S(k+1)=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to express the summation $S(k+1)$ in terms of $S(k).$\n\nLet ${a}_{i}$ for $i\\ge 0$ be a sequence, and let $S(k)$ denote the sum of the first $k+1$ terms.\n\n$$\nS(k)={\\sum }_{i=0}^{k}{a}_{i}\n$$\n\nWe can always express $S(k+1)$ in terms of $S(k)$ by writing the last term on its own, as follows: \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=0}^{k+1}{a}_{i}=({\\sum }_{i=0}^{k}{a}_{i})+{a}_{k+1}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have ${a}_{i}=2-i.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{k+1}=2-(k+1)=1-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=0}^{k+1}(2-i)=({\\sum }_{i=0}^{k}(2-i))+(1-k),\n$$\n\nwhich we can write as \n\n$$\nS(k+1)=S(k)+1-k.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b1d7e221-6d8a-5eb3-939e-8ee5b0d490ae"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b1d7e221-6d8a-5eb3-939e-8ee5b0d490ae" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1d7e221-6d8a-5eb3-939e-8ee5b0d490ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e236beed-88b1-54af-907e-d7f0041cdfc9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5a169e12-7e4c-5e25-8147-73aad745a028" "answer-e315aeb0-337d-5bff-99f7-dec0f030ecf3" "answer-e236beed-88b1-54af-907e-d7f0041cdfc9" "answer-b6f16e45-756f-5226-9e97-b731586b808a" "answer-e8ab77ee-20d9-58f6-9099-417dec1cb15f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a169e12-7e4c-5e25-8147-73aad745a028" :answer/id #uuid "5a169e12-7e4c-5e25-8147-73aad745a028" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-S(k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e315aeb0-337d-5bff-99f7-dec0f030ecf3" :answer/id #uuid "e315aeb0-337d-5bff-99f7-dec0f030ecf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-S(k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e236beed-88b1-54af-907e-d7f0041cdfc9" :answer/id #uuid "e236beed-88b1-54af-907e-d7f0041cdfc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "S(k)+1-k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-